    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nSometimes, mini.completion throws this error while trying to show the signature window:\n\n```\n                     Error executing vim.schedule lua callback: .../share/nvim/lazy/mini.completion/lua/mini/completion.lua:1620: attempt to perform arithmetic on a nil value\nstack traceback:\n\t.../share/nvim/lazy/mini.completion/lua/mini/completion.lua:1620: in function 'processor'\n\t.../share/nvim/lazy/mini.completion/lua/mini/completion.lua:1115: in function 'process_lsp_response'\n\t.../share/nvim/lazy/mini.completion/lua/mini/completion.lua:1566: in function 'signature_window_lines'\n\t.../share/nvim/lazy/mini.completion/lua/mini/completion.lua:1524: in function 'show_signature_window'\n\t.../share/nvim/lazy/mini.completion/lua/mini/completion.lua:1514: in function 'handler'\n\t.../Cellar/neovim/0.11.1/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp.lua:1247: in function 'handler'\n\t.../neovim/0.11.1/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/client.lua:682: in function ''\n\tvim/_editor.lua: in function <vim/_editor.lua:0>\n```\n\n### Reproduction\n\nThe reproduction requires that you install mini.completion and the Julia LSP. After that, if you type:\n\n```\nget(\n```\n\nYou will get the error while trying to complete the signature for the function `get`.",
