        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nI have not reproduced it (because it requires installing both Julia and its LSP server. It might take a while for me to do so.\n\nIn the meantime, are you comfortable applying patch to the local installation of the 'mini.nvim' / 'mini.completion'? If yes, could you please try making this change and see if it fixes the issue:\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/lua/mini/completion.lua b/lua/mini/completion.lua\nindex 548b8e59..ac723871 100644\n--- a/lua/mini/completion.lua\n+++ b/lua/mini/completion.lua\n@@ -1617,7 +1617,7 @@ H.process_signature_response = function(response)\n     local label_is_string = type(param_label) == 'string'\n     res.hl_range = label_is_string and { res.label:find(param_label, 1, true) } or (param_label or {})\n     -- - Make zero-indexed and end-exclusive\n-    res.hl_range[1] = res.hl_range[1] - (label_is_string and 1 or 0)\n+    if res.hl_range[1] ~= nil then res.hl_range[1] = res.hl_range[1] - (label_is_string and 1 or 0) end\n   end\n \n   -- Return nested table because this will be a second argument of\n```\n\n(I.e. find [this line](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/8ca3965e68edfee5f438d4063f5adf5afa255884/lua/mini/completion.lua#L1620) in your local installation of 'mini.nvim' / 'mini.completion' and change it to `    if res.hl_range[1] ~= nil then res.hl_range[1] = res.hl_range[1] - (label_is_string and 1 or 0) end`)",
