        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I've managed to reproduce and the patch does indeed fix the issue.\n\nThe problem here, though, is the LSP server itself, as it returns not really correct data structure for at least one of the signatures:\n\n```\n{\n  documentation = \"\",\n  label = \"get(::Base.EnvDict, k::Core.AbstractString, def::Core.Any) in Base at /base/env.jl:165\",\n  parameters = {\n    { documentation = \"Base.EnvDict\", label = \"#unused#\" },\n    { documentation = \"Core.AbstractString\", label = \"k\" },\n    { documentation = \"Core.Any\", label = \"def\"}\n  }\n}\n```\n\n[Per LSP specification](https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/specifications/lsp/3.17/specification/#parameterInformation), the string parameter `label` should be a substring of its containing signature `label`. Here \"#unused#\" is not a substring.\n\nI'll consider updating the 'mini.completion' to account for that, but my suggestion would be to raise this issue with Julia's LSP server in the first place.",
